cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  OpenTallas: an evidence-gated study of model-specific mask-ROM
  inference silicon
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it, and please cite what the
  repository actually establishes. Its headline throughput and cost
  figures are deterministic ANALYTICAL model outputs, not measurements of
  hardware. No OpenTallas silicon exists: there is no tapeout, no
  fabricated device, no foundry signoff, and no benchmark on real
  hardware. Physical-design results come from ASAP7, a predictive and
  non-manufacturable academic PDK.

  The repository tracks its own readiness with a 19-rung gate board.
  Running `python3 tools/check_redesign_gates.py` takes under a second
  and prints the current state; at the time of writing 9 of 19 rungs and
  1 of 4 terminal gates pass. Gate C3 -- that the cycle model and the
  analytical model agree on the binding constraint -- is FAILING, and it
  bears directly on the headline comparison. See
  docs/REPRODUCIBILITY.md for what an outside reader can and cannot
  re-derive.
type: software
authors:
