abstract: >-
  OpenTallas asks what it would take to make model-specific ROM
  inference open and inspectable: weights fabricated into mask ROM rather
  than streamed from HBM, evaluated against a conventional HBM/GPU
  comparator under a shared ABI.

  The repository connects model accounting, an analytical architecture
  study, a backend-neutral compiler and runtime with a cycle model,
  synthesizable reference RTL, and open-PDK physical and circuit
  experiments into one evidence chain in which prose figures are bound by
  digest to the artifacts that produced them.

  Its distinguishing feature is that it is gated against itself rather
  than presented as finished. Claims are separated by evidence class;
  absence of evidence is recorded as failure rather than as "not
  evaluable"; source-binding digests make a stale artifact inadmissible;
  and the repository publishes its own post-mortems, including one
  titled "how the accelerator came to be 44,000x too slow". Readers are
  invited to check the numbers, and the tooling to do so is included.
